invariant: INV-16
file: quic_packet.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: byte_in_use builds its mask from the borrow itself, without the
  volatile read. A compiler then knows the mask is all ones or zero, and
  clang for rv32imac writes quic_pn_read's choice by it as a branch on
  the sign of i - pn_len, the encoded length RFC 9001 section 9.5 makes a
  secret (rfc9001.txt:2110-2112, docs/decisions.md 125). Every test
  passes on it, because the value is the same. lint-wide-multiply counts
  quic_packet.c's conditional branches, and the rv32imac spec then reads
  more than its ceiling.

--- old
    uint32_t borrow = opaque;
--- new
    uint32_t borrow = ((uint32_t)i - (uint32_t)pn_len) >> 31;
